{"title":"2024 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!!!!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!!!!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_(Goes_through_full_thought_process)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Quick_solution)_by_Parshwa\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Quick solution) by Parshwa</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve_(easy_to_understand)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve (easy to understand)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#2_minute_solve_(fast_and_elegant)_by_MegaMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">2 minute solve (fast and elegant) by MegaMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution-_(Extremely_Simple_Triangle_Theories!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution- (Extremely Simple Triangle Theories!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jean has made a piece of stained glass art in the shape of two mountains, as shown in the figure below. One mountain peak is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet high while the other peak is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet high. Each peak forms a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle, and the straight sides form a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle with the ground. The artwork has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d0ae020c85a8c5c48aeff0a6b320b766b4278c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$183$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> square feet. The sides of the mountain meet at an intersection point near the center of the artwork, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> feet above the ground. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42ab3016933ac8484ed7f75ac9cb6e1cc53f2718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/062be4008fc995e68ebbe56afa0a90b07160a7d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(.3cm); filldraw((0,0)--(8,8)--(11,5)--(18,12)--(30,0)--cycle,gray(0.7),linewidth(1)); draw((-1,0)--(-1,8),linewidth(.75)); draw((-1.4,0)--(-.6,0),linewidth(.75)); draw((-1.4,8)--(-.6,8),linewidth(.75)); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,(-1,4),W); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,(31,6),E); draw((-1,8)--(8,8),dashed); draw((31,0)--(31,12),linewidth(.75)); draw((30.6,0)--(31.4,0),linewidth(.75)); draw((30.6,12)--(31.4,12),linewidth(.75)); draw((31,12)--(18,12),dashed); label(&quot;$45^{\\circ}$&quot;,(.75,0),NE,fontsize(10pt)); label(&quot;$45^{\\circ}$&quot;,(29.25,0),NW,fontsize(10pt)); draw((8,8)--(7.5,7.5)--(8,7)--(8.5,7.5)--cycle); draw((18,12)--(17.5,11.5)--(18,11)--(18.5,11.5)--cycle); draw((11,5)--(11,0),dashed); label(&quot;$h$&quot;,(11,2.5),E); [/asy]\" width=\"502\" height=\"175\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c87f1560571d0f22725b6a084c02e939c1ff01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 4\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 5\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"400\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Extend the \"inner part\" of the mountain so that the image is two right triangles that overlap in a third right triangle as shown. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88bf4e27a470961cc074edc3adc9d53475fc71e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(.2cm); draw((0,0)--(8,8)--(11,5)--(18,12)--(30,0)--cycle,linewidth(1)); draw((11,5)--(6, 0)--(16, 0)--cycle,linewidth(0.5)); label(&quot;$8\\sqrt{2}$&quot;,(4,4),NW); label(&quot;$12\\sqrt{2}$&quot;,(24,6),NE); draw((8,8)--(7.5,7.5)--(8,7)--(8.5,7.5)--cycle); draw((18,12)--(17.5,11.5)--(18,11)--(18.5,11.5)--cycle); draw((11,5)--(11,0),dashed); label(&quot;$h$&quot;,(11,2.5),E); [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"118\" />\nThe side length of the largest right triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5741dea84f46be1cc04d2ccbb30a6fed7e67aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12\\sqrt{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"23\" /> which means its area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f6fc67c4374b3f79b8bd713e801b9b7d34d2f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> Similarly, the area of the second largest right triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> (the side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ada42b1f945fea827946e80d64ab5f27e7ba8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />), and the area of the overlap is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319c4d6557b81962a2076f2017878709cf698551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> (the side length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5b5fe4f4dd718e0cbbe350909a3e16ced427aa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"21\" />). Because the right triangles have a side ratio of 1:1:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />.Thus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da33465ebae23a898b76506cd66992f6ff48089f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[144+64-h^2=183,\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" />\nwhich means that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/1/75177103789c611b0aef5e60ec8b46c73b85b7b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathbf{(B)}\\text{ 5}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~BS2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/OwJvuq6F7sQ\">https://youtu.be/OwJvuq6F7sQ</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/29xcfUcmTgg\">https://youtu.be/29xcfUcmTgg</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.21.21.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!!!!!!)\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!!!!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!!!!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/BaE00H2SHQM?si=793ml6R_qT79h-aI&amp;t=7651\">https://youtu.be/BaE00H2SHQM?si=793ml6R_qT79h-aI&amp;t=7651</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_.28Goes_through_full_thought_process.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_(Goes_through_full_thought_process)\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DL83nznn3gM\">https://youtu.be/DL83nznn3gM</a>\n</p><p>~mr_mathman\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5ZIFnqymdDQ?si=D8pGHQYbzJ_eMsEy&amp;t=3678\">https://youtu.be/5ZIFnqymdDQ?si=D8pGHQYbzJ_eMsEy&amp;t=3678</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Quick_solution.29_by_Parshwa\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Quick_solution)_by_Parshwa\">Video Solution (Quick solution) by Parshwa</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Quick solution) by Parshwa\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ky-NVrOv4ew\">https://youtu.be/Ky-NVrOv4ew</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve_.28easy_to_understand.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve_(easy_to_understand)\">Video Solution by Power Solve (easy to understand)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve (easy to understand)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></